        {
          "path": "_m/9/t/9/p/fort-lowell-tucson-arizona-wp/fort-lowell-park-entra.jpg",
          "filename": "Tucson-Fort Lowell Park 1873-1891.JPG",
          "caption": "The Fort Lowell Park entrance is located at 2900 N Craycroft Rd. in Tucson, Az.. Fort Lowell was a United States Army post which was active from 1873 to 1891 on the outskirts of Tucson, Arizona. It is the historical setting of the 1957-1958 syndicated Western television series, Boots and Saddles, starring John M. Pickard, Patrick McVey, and Gardner McKay. The park is now owned by the city of Tucson and was listed in the National Register of Historic Places in 1978, ref.: #78003358.",
          "alt": "The Fort Lowell Park entrance is located at 2900 N Craycroft Rd. in Tucson, Az.. Fort Lowell was a United States Army post which was active from 1873 to 1891 on the outskirts of Tucson, Arizona. It is the historical setting of the 1957-1958 syndicated Western television series, Boots and Saddles, starring John M. Pickard, Patrick McVey, and Gardner McKay. The park is now owned by the city of Tucson and was listed in the National Register of Historic Places in 1978, ref.: #78003358.",
